gosh seam 19: Each of the core's domains has tests of its own: what its factoring must not change.

For:   REQ21/SHAPE-1: "no byte of the protocol changes, and no behaviour". The factoring (seams 12
       to 18) moved and renamed the core's code; only the cipher had tests of its own (seam 13),
       and gosh's check ran none of the core's. Each domain now has one, run by the check's
       tests of each laid-out core domain (tools/check.sh).
What:  Five tests are added, each under its domain's imp/, with gosh's testing library (vendor/facts),
       each seen to fail with its domain broken once and to pass as it is:
       - the transport (imp/transport-test.cc): an instruction made into fragments no larger than
         the MTU, only the last final; a fragment's bytes read back as itself; the fragments, in any
         order, put together as the instruction; compression there and back; a port range parsed,
         and what is not one refused;
       - state synchronisation (imp/statesync-test.cc): the user's stream, its diff applied; one
         terminal's diff from another making the other show the same (the core's compare);
       - the terminal (imp/terminal-test.cc): the parser's prints and its dispatch of a control
         sequence; printed text, CR LF and the cursor in the framebuffer; a title's prefix;
       - the programs (imp/overlay-test.cc): the title engine's prefix; a notification drawn;
       - the utilities (imp/util-test.cc): swrite writes all; the frozen timestamp; a locale's
         variable said.
       The terminal's three set the locale C.UTF-8, as the core's programs refuse any other.
Where: src/{network,statesync,terminal,frontend,util}/Makefile.am; imp/*-test.cc in each.
Kind:  adds tests only; nothing of the core's own code changes.
From:  gosh's own, 2026-11-27 (the owner: "go ahead and add tests for the new domains").
